From 0214407387fafcfaf6d9e9609491ca1f68d34cd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt C <latentcollapse@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:22:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 39/45] compaction: only the newest NeuraJL state note reaches
 the model; custom messages count toward the kept tail

tin3 compacted 255 times, after nearly every call for its last hour. A
neurajl_state note is written after every compaction and none was ever
dropped; a kept tail spanning several compactions carried a stack of them
(79k characters in one), and findCutPoint counted only entry.type ===
"message", so the tail outgrew keepRecentTokens and the next request was
already over the trigger. Older notes are now skipped at context assembly,
as older harness digests are, and custom messages count toward the kept
budget. Red controls: both new build-context tests and the findCutPoint
test fail without their fix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
